  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe #2435 wall-law refusal in `ride_loops` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs`) said that a chamfer \"would ride into the part\". It said this also when the chamfer source was the stock and no part was near. #2483 found this with a tilted stock-source chamfer.\n\n`ride_loops` does not know the source: the caller (`crates/app/src/operation/material_source.rs`) gives it two sections only. Thus the text now uses a word that fits the two cases, as the issue permits:\n\n- Before: `... a 1 mm chamfer there would ride into the part; lower the width or pick the edges to break`\n- After: `... a 1 mm chamfer there would ride into the material under it; lower the width or pick the edges to break`\n\nThe doc comment of `ride_loops` says the same. No geometry, no refusal condition and no API changes.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_wall_farther_than_the_width_refuses_by_name` (camcraft-motion lib). It now also asserts:\n- the text contains `would ride into the material under it;`;\n- the text does not contain `part`.\n\nWith the old text the test fails (`... would ride into the part; lower ...`). With the new text the 4 `chamfer_ride` tests pass.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, Linux, 12 cores, another build running on the box):\n- `motion suites: lib`: ok (854 s; the gate lists 11 adaptive tests over 60 s on this loaded box, none touched here).\n- `app suites: chamfer_modelled_edge`: ok.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNo other test, doc or skill asserts or quotes the old text (`git grep \"ride into\"`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run in the app or through MCP. The refusal reaches the user as the same `GenError::At` with the same location.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Branch base: `upstream/main`. No context scout ran; this session did its own searches.\n\nChangelog: The 2D chamfer refusal for an edge with no wall under it no longer says \"part\" when the chamfer source is the stock.\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #2521\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
